cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FCCgroup app
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the
  accompanying publication listed under `preferred-citation`.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anguera Sempere
    given-names: Albert
    affiliation: Food Packaging Forum Foundation
  - family-names: Wiesinger
    given-names: Helene
    affiliation: Food Packaging Forum Foundation
  - name: Food Packaging Forum Foundation
    city: Zurich
    country: CH
    website: 'https://www.foodpackagingforum.org/'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Food-Packaging-Forum/FCCgroup-app'
url: 'https://github.com/Food-Packaging-Forum/FCCgroup-app'
abstract: >-
  A Streamlit web application for screening chemicals against the Food Packaging
  Forum's food contact chemical resources. It identifies whether each input
  chemical is a known food contact chemical (FCCdb, FCCmigex), enriches it with
  its FCCprio priority tier and hazard flags, and assigns structural priority
  groups using the fccgroup Python package.
keywords:
  - food contact chemicals
  - chemical grouping
  - chemical prioritization
  - read-across
  - SMARTS
  - cheminformatics
  - streamlit
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
